---
import PixelEdges from "./PixelEdges.astro"
---

<section class="why">
    <PixelEdges left="tall" right="cluster" />
    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <span class="eyebrow">Why we exist</span>
            <h2>Every team automated<br />its own corner.</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="text">
            <p>
                Kestra started in 2019 at Leroy Merlin, Europe's largest DIY
                retailer, where every team automated its own corner with its own
                tool and no one could see or control the whole. Data had its
                scheduler, infrastructure its scripts, operations its runbooks.
                When something broke between them, no one owned it.
            </p>
            <p>
                We built one control plane for all of it. Every flow, schedule,
                trigger and approval lives there, versioned and audited, while
                the work still runs in the databases, clouds, scripts and tools
                teams already have. Kestra Enterprise and Kestra Cloud add what
                mission-critical workflows need: security, governance, high
                availability and 24/7 support. A five-person team running
                critical workflows needs that as much as a global bank does.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
    @use "./style/section" as *;

    .why {
        @include section;
        position: relative;
        background: var(--ks-background-body);

        .container {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
            gap: 4rem;

            @include media-breakpoint-down(lg) {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                gap: 1.5rem;
            }
        }
    }

    header {
        align-self: start;
        position: sticky;
        top: 7rem;

        @include media-breakpoint-down(lg) {
            position: static;
        }
    }

    .eyebrow {
        @include eyebrow;
    }

    h2 {
        @include title;
    }

    .text {
        p {
            margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
            font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.6vw, 1.375rem);
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: var(--ks-content-secondary);

            &:first-child {
                color: var(--ks-content-primary);
            }
        }
    }
</style>
